cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Pianura in academic work, please cite the paper that describes
  the original JUSE and the UniBot project (preferred citation below).
type: software
title: "Pianura Sim: a 2D simulator for differential-drive robots"
abstract: >-
  A 2D simulator for teaching and research on mobile robots and swarms:
  differential-drive kinematics, infrared, bump and floor sensors computed
  by ray casting, radio between robots, a simulated clock, debug drawings,
  and remote control over UDP from Python and MATLAB. Evolved from JUSE
  (Java UniBot Simulation Environment, University of Bologna, 2008-2011).
authors:
